NAME
    web-analyze-pw - deeply inspect one browser page using Playwright

SYNOPSIS
    web-analyze-pw <http(s)-url> [--headless] [--output <new-directory>]
        [--max-steps <1..200>] [--settle-ms <100..10000>]
        [--observe-ms <0..3600000>]

DESCRIPTION
    Launch the Chromium browser paired with the installed Playwright package.
    The literal 'playwright' command is resolved using the effective PATH, not
    through a configured or hardcoded filesystem path. Its Node runtime provides
    the corresponding Playwright module and browser-cache location.

    The default visible browser loads the URL and wheel-scrolls down and back up
    through the dominant document or nested scrollable container. Each observed
    position is captured as page DOM HTML and a viewport PNG. Extra evidence
    includes timestamped JSONL network/console/navigation/DOM-mutation/scroll/
    performance events, trace.zip and a final native Chromium MHTML snapshot.

    Pages that mount/virtualize only part of a large document, including ChatGPT
    shared conversations, cannot be reconstructed completely from one snapshot.
    A capture describes only the observed mounted DOM at its recorded position.

OPTIONS
    --headless           Do not open a visible browser window.
    --output DIR         Write to a NEW directory. Existing directories fail.
    --max-steps N        Maximum wheel actions per direction; default 80.
    --settle-ms N        Pause after wheel action; default 500 milliseconds.
    --observe-ms N       Extra observation time after sweep; default 0.

OUTPUT
    New private directory (0700), files (0600):
        events.jsonl     Sequenced observations with UTC/monotonic timestamps.
        summary.json     URL, timing, captures, partial/failure status.
        0000-*.html      Current mounted HTML at each checkpoint.
        0000-*.png       Corresponding viewport screenshots.
        trace.zip        Playwright trace with snapshots and screenshots.
        final.mhtml      Best-effort native CDP MHTML of FINAL mounted DOM.

    Sensitive page/session data can be present in HTML, screenshots, MHTML or
    trace. Do not upload or publish these artifacts without reviewing them.
    Events intentionally omit request bodies, headers, cookies and typed values.
    URL query/fragment values are redacted. URL paths are not redacted.

DEPENDENCIES
    'node' and the m-managed 'playwright' command must be available on PATH;
    install 'pkg install playwright' and 'playwright install chromium' first.
    The Node API is resolved from the installed Playwright CLI process, with
    no assumption about the package's physical installation directory.
    No TLS validation or Chromium sandbox bypass is used.

EXIT STATUS
    0   Completed successfully.
    1   Invalid arguments.
    2   Playwright command failed.
    3   Node module probe unavailable.
    4   Playwright Node module not found.
    5   Playwright API unavailable.
    6   Chromium launch failed (browser may need installation).
    7   Navigation failed.
    8   Other analysis/output failure.

EXAMPLE
    web-analyze-pw \
      https://chatgpt.com/share/6ad1c0d5-49ec-83eb-a79b-85b04b938835 \
      --headless --output ./chatgpt-share-evidence

